     "texto": [
      "In **我给你一个苹果**, the order is **person + 给 + recipient + thing**: «I give you an apple». If you want to stress that you're giving a present, you can also say **送给** + person + thing.",
      "In Chinese, 给 can also appear before the person who receives a call or help; context makes its role clear."
